    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371-a1">

                <pb facs="0509" n="429" xml:id="pg429"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor de Osma to Mr. Dudley.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Lima</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May
                                21, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: In reference to the interviews
                    your excellency and I have had regarding the claim of J. H. Hayball, supported
                    by your legation, I have the pleasure to state to your excellency that my
                    Government has no objections to adjust the matter by a payment of 8,000
                    soles.</p>
                <p>Your excellency will please to consider this decision as a proof of the sincere
                    good feeling existing in the relations between the two Governments, without this
                    settlement being in any wise considered as a precedent for the adjustment of
                    other cases.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. de Osma.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
